json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-337533" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-337533" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-337533" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x{e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "x{e}^{6x}"] ["math" "{e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "{e}^{6x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-337533" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x{e}^{6x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\  & =6{e}^{-3x}(\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{-3x}({e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =3+3{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =3+3{e}^{-6x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3+3{e}^{-6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ce98d1f36ea22fc85e5889cab20bb9f5d1f93c570e96e4e7b5b69647724e675"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "u(x){e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "u(x){e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "u(x){e}^{3x}"] ["math" "u(x){e}^{6x}"] ["math" "u(x){e}^{9x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "u(x){e}^{3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "1-x{e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}"] ["math" "3x-{e}^{-6x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "3x{e}^{3x}-{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "{e}^{3x}-x{e}^{-3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-338129" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-352892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=2{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-352892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-5x})}^{′}+5(u{e}^{-5x}) & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-5u{e}^{-5x}+5u{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-352892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ce98d1f36ea22fc85e5889cab20bb9f5d1f93c570e96e4e7b5b69647724e675"} {"question" "q-352892" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057172/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd79d6b321a85fbbec02854dabf978c76ed12a3f86405977fc73403e677555bc"} {"question" "q-352892" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "u(x){e}^{-5x